window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-bec1e26cb654a758"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"codex-security-plugin-quickstart\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex-security\">Codex Security 插件快速入门</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>安装 Codex Security 插件，对本地代码库运行一次标准扫描，然后审阅发现项。扫描不会更改源代码，并会保存一份包含证据和修复指导的报告。</p> <p>本页介绍桌面应用或 Codex CLI 中的 Codex Security 插件。如果要在 Codex cloud 中扫描已连接的 GitHub 代码库，请从插件市场安装单独的 <strong>Codex Security Cloud</strong> 插件。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">云端设置</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"install-the-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">安装插件</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>打开 <a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT 桌面应用中的 Codex</a>。</li> <li>打开 <strong>Plugins（插件）</strong>，搜索 <strong>Codex Security</strong>，或使用下面的按钮：</li> </ol> <p>安装 Codex Security 插件 — 应用链接: <code>codex://plugins/install/codex-security?marketplace=openai-curated</code></p> <ol> <li>确认插件已启用，然后在侧边栏中打开 <strong>Security（安全）</strong>。</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>在终端中进入要评估的代码库，并启动 Codex：</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>输入 <code>/plugins</code>，搜索 <strong>Codex Security</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Install plugin（安装插件）</strong>。</li> <li>输入 <code>/new</code>，为该代码库开始新的聊天。</li> </ol> <p>如果桌面应用的侧边栏中没有显示 <strong>Security（安全）</strong>，请确认已选中 <strong>Codex</strong>，且插件已启用。必要时更新应用和插件，并确认工作区管理员是否允许使用该插件。</p> <p><a id=\"run-your-first-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">运行第一次扫描</h2> <p>为获得较好的扫描质量，请使用 <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code>，并选择 <code>xhigh</code> 推理强度。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> <p>截图未离线保存: Codex Security 工作台显示代码库扫描开始前的新建扫描设置</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 开始扫描前，先选择代码库并配置新的安全扫描。 </figcaption> <ol> <li>打开扫描设置</li> </ol> <p>在侧边栏中选择 <strong>Security（安全）</strong>，打开 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>+ Scan（新建扫描）</strong>。</p> <ol> <li>选择代码库和扫描区域</li> </ol> <p>选择一个已有代码库，或使用其他文件夹。选择 <strong>Codebase（代码库）</strong>，保持 <strong>Deep scan（深度扫描）</strong>关闭，然后选择整个代码库或一个文件夹。请确认分支和修订版本指向你要扫描的代码。</p> <ol> <li>添加安全上下文</li> </ol> <p>选择模型和推理强度。只有在需要描述攻击途径、安全敏感区域或可指导审查的代码库细节时，才打开 <strong>Additional context（补充上下文）</strong>。</p> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: Codex Security 扫描设置已启用补充上下文，并显示攻击途径、重点区域和安全指导示例</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 开启补充上下文，以描述攻击途径、重点区域和相关安全指导。 </figcaption> <ol> <li>启动扫描</li> </ol> <p>选择 <strong>Start scan（开始扫描）</strong>，并在 Security 工作台中跟踪扫描阶段。选择 <strong>View activity（查看活动）</strong>可查看执行扫描的 Codex 任务。</p> <ol> <li>审阅结果</li> </ol> <p>打开已完成的扫描，检查发现项、覆盖范围和可用报告文件。使用 <strong>Findings（发现项）</strong>跨扫描审阅问题，或使用 <strong>Repositories（代码库）</strong>查看代码库的扫描历史。</p> <blockquote> <p>截图未离线保存: 已完成的 Codex Security 扫描在原生工作台中显示发现项</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> 在 Security 工作台中审阅扫描结果、发现项和覆盖范围。 </figcaption> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>请求标准扫描</li> </ol> <p>在新的聊天中发送以下提示：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   对当前代码库运行 Codex Security 扫描。\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>等待扫描完成</li> </ol> <p>Codex 会在终端中运行扫描，不会打开扫描设置工作区。请让任务继续运行，直到 Codex 报告扫描完成。如果 Codex 指出配置限制，请先审阅该限制和建议的具体更改，再决定是否批准配置更新。</p> <ol> <li>审阅结果</li> </ol> <p>先查看终端中的摘要，然后打开生成的 <code>report.md</code> 查看完整结果。</p> <p><a id=\"interpret-the-result\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">解读结果</h2> <p>先检查目标和修订版本，然后查看已审查和延期审查的区域。扫描即使完成，也可能存在覆盖缺口。扫描没有报告发现项，并不意味着它已经排除了所有漏洞。</p> <p>打开某项发现，阅读其源代码证据、攻击者所需条件、验证方式和剩余的不确定性。验证可以基于源代码分析，而不必运行复现程序。请依据记录的方法和证据，判断该问题是否适用于你的系统。</p> <p><a id=\"what-the-scan-creates\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">扫描会生成什么</h2> <p>在桌面应用中，已完成的扫描会保留在 <strong>Scans（扫描）</strong>中。在 Codex CLI 中，请使用对话里报告的扫描目录。打开 <code>report.md</code> 查看易读的结果。<code>findings/</code> 下的详细漏洞报告和 <code>hardening/</code> 下的设计提案均为可选输出，可以按需请求。</p> <p>该目录还包含供工具和自动化使用的 <code>scan-manifest.json</code>、<code>findings.json</code> 和 <code>coverage.json</code>。分享或归档时，请将目录完整保留，以便报告链接继续有效。</p> <p><a id=\"choose-your-next-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">选择下一步工作流</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">配置范围和安全上下文</a>以准备下一次扫描，或<a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">审查代码更改</a>。</li> <li>接受某项发现的证据后，可以<a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">修复并验证发现项</a>，或<a href=\"#/article/a-2908d6b44ee04c2d\">在问题跟踪系统中跟踪它</a>。</li> </ul> <p>如需了解其他扫描模式和工作流，请返回 <a href=\"#/article/a-d5a186b7366ebd04\">Codex Security 概览</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"codex-security-plugin-quickstart\">Codex Security plugin quickstart</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Install the Codex Security plugin, run a standard scan of a local repository, and review its findings. The scan leaves your source unchanged and saves a report with evidence and remediation guidance.</p> <p>This page covers the Codex Security plugin in the desktop app or Codex CLI. To scan a connected GitHub repository in Codex cloud, install the separate <strong>Codex Security Cloud</strong> plugin from the plugin marketplace. See <a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">Cloud setup</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"install-the-plugin\">Install the plugin</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>Open <a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">Codex in the ChatGPT desktop app</a>.</li> <li>Open <strong>Plugins</strong>, search for <strong>Codex Security</strong>, or use the button below:</li> </ol> <p>Install the Codex Security plugin — App link: <code>codex://plugins/install/codex-security?marketplace=openai-curated</code></p> <ol> <li>Confirm the plugin is enabled, then open <strong>Security</strong> in the sidebar.</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>In your terminal, go to the repository you want to assess and start Codex:</li> </ol> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">   codex\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Enter <code>/plugins</code>, search for <strong>Codex Security</strong>, and select <strong>Install plugin</strong>.</li> <li>Enter <code>/new</code> to start a new chat for the repository.</li> </ol> <p>If <strong>Security</strong> doesn't appear in the desktop-app sidebar, confirm that <strong>Codex</strong> is selected and the plugin is enabled. Update the app and plugin if needed, and check whether your workspace administrator allows the plugin.</p> <h2 id=\"run-your-first-scan\">Run your first scan</h2> <p>For the best scan quality, use <code>gpt-5.6-sol</code> with <code>xhigh</code> reasoning effort.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Native Codex Security workbench showing the new scan setup before a repository scan starts</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Choose a repository and configure a new security scan before you start it. </figcaption> <ol> <li>Open the scan setup</li> </ol> <p>Select <strong>Security</strong> in the sidebar, open <strong>Scans</strong>, and select <strong>+ Scan</strong>.</p> <ol> <li>Choose the codebase and scan area</li> </ol> <p>Select an existing repository or use another folder. Choose <strong>Codebase</strong>, leave <strong>Deep scan</strong> off, and select the entire repository or one folder. Confirm that the branch and revision identify the code you intended to scan.</p> <ol> <li>Add security context</li> </ol> <p>Choose the model and reasoning effort. Open <strong>Additional context</strong> only when you need to describe an attack vector, security-sensitive area, or repository detail that should guide the review.</p> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Native Codex Security scan setup with additional context enabled and example attack vectors, focus areas, and security guidance</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Turn on additional context to describe attack vectors, focus areas, and relevant security guidance. </figcaption> <ol> <li>Start the scan</li> </ol> <p>Select <strong>Start scan</strong> and follow the scan phases in the Security workbench. Select <strong>View activity</strong> to inspect the Codex task that performs the scan.</p> <ol> <li>Review the result</li> </ol> <p>Open the completed scan to inspect findings, coverage, and available report artifacts. Use <strong>Findings</strong> to review issues across scans or <strong>Repositories</strong> to inspect a repository's scan history.</p> <blockquote> <p>Screenshot not stored offline: Completed Codex Security scan showing findings in the native workbench</p> </blockquote> <figcaption> Review scan results, findings, and coverage in the Security workbench. </figcaption> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <ol> <li>Ask for a standard scan</li> </ol> <p>Send this prompt in the new chat:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">   Run a Codex Security scan on this repository.\n</code></pre> <ol> <li>Let the scan finish</li> </ol> <p>Codex runs the scan in the terminal without opening a setup workspace. Keep the task running until Codex reports that it is complete. If Codex identifies a configuration limitation, review the limitation and the exact proposed change before you approve a configuration update.</p> <ol> <li>Review the result</li> </ol> <p>Review the summary in the terminal, then open the generated <code>report.md</code> for the complete result.</p> <h2 id=\"interpret-the-result\">Interpret the result</h2> <p>Check the target and revision first. Then read which areas were reviewed and which were deferred. A completed scan can still have coverage gaps. A review that reports no findings hasn't necessarily ruled out every vulnerability.</p> <p>Open a finding and read its source evidence, attacker prerequisites, validation, and remaining uncertainty. Validation can use source analysis without running a reproducer. Use the recorded method and evidence to decide whether the issue applies to your system.</p> <h2 id=\"what-the-scan-creates\">What the scan creates</h2> <p>In the desktop app, completed scans remain in <strong>Scans</strong>. In Codex CLI, use the scan directory reported in the conversation. Open <code>report.md</code> for the readable result. Detailed vulnerability reports under <code>findings/</code> and design proposals under <code>hardening/</code> are optional outputs you can request.</p> <p>The directory also contains <code>scan-manifest.json</code>, <code>findings.json</code>, and <code>coverage.json</code> for tools and automation. Keep it together when sharing or archiving results so the report's links continue to work.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-your-next-workflow\">Choose your next workflow</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-52ffdad46ad27a2b\">Configure scope and security context</a> for the next scan, or <a href=\"#/article/a-06694345b68735af\">review a code change</a>.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-44471eb3eae1b363\">Fix and verify a finding</a> after you accept its evidence, or <a href=\"#/article/a-2908d6b44ee04c2d\">track it in an issue</a>.</li> </ul> <p>For other scan modes and workflows, return to the <a href=\"#/article/a-d5a186b7366ebd04\">Codex Security overview</a>.</p>"};
